{
  // Enforces Rule 14.1 (`.agents/rules/03-backend-data.md`) where it matters.
  //
  // `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` is what makes `const [row] = await db.select()`
  // an error instead of a lie: without it TypeScript types the destructured
  // element as present, so a lookup that finds nothing is inferred as always
  // finding something and the guard the rule asks for is unenforceable.
  //
  // It is not enabled in the root tsconfig because it is the wrong tool for
  // dense numeric arrays and fixture-driven tests — the SHA-256 word array in
  // `theme-compiler-hasher.ts` alone would need 44 non-null assertions for no
  // safety gain. `npm run typecheck:data` therefore compiles the whole program
  // with the flag on but only *reports* the data-access layer, which is where
  // an absent row is a real failure mode.
  //
  // Widen the filter in `scripts/typecheck-data-layer.mjs` as other areas are
  // brought up to it.
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true
  }
}
